# Cloudflare Pages headers for playprofessorpaws.com
#
# Place at the REPO ROOT of professorpaws-site (Cloudflare Pages reads `/_headers`).
# GitHub Pages ignores this file, so it is safe to commit before the hosting cutover.
#
# WHY: the two token pages declare `frame-ancestors 'none'` in a <meta> CSP, and the spec makes
# frame-ancestors (and X-Frame-Options) INERT in meta — they are header-only. Verified live: both
# pages currently return NO X-Frame-Options, NO CSP header, and NO Referrer-Policy.

# --- Every page: baseline.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# --- The two TOKEN pages. Three things the rest of the site does not need.
#
# 1. A REAL CSP header, mirroring each page's existing meta CSP exactly so nothing breaks — the only
#    change is that frame-ancestors now actually applies.
# 2. Referrer-Policy: no-referrer. These URLs CARRY A ONE-TIME TOKEN. Anything less than no-referrer
#    can put that token in a Referer header.
# 3. Cache-Control: no-store. Live today they return `max-age=600`, so a token-bearing page is
#    cacheable for ten minutes — on a shared family device, that is the token sitting in cache.
/confirm.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; form-action https://mlokvzsjrrwlcejjonck.supabase.co; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
  Pragma: no-cache

/reset.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cache-Control: no-store, no-cache, must-revalidate, private
  Pragma: no-cache
